<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghilzai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ghilzai Afghans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ghilzai are a large Pashtun tribal confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. Persecuted for their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> faith, the Ghilzai of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirwais-hotak">Mir Wais</a> and in 1722 captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>, expelled them from Isfahan in 1729.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghilzai.jpg" alt="Ghilzai" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Burke (1843-1900) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sirdar_Habibullah_Gilzai_and_other_Khans_in_1879-80.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
